Package: VisitationR
Title: Estimate Pollinator Visitation Rates from Seed Set Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ignasi", "Bartomeus",
           , "nachobartomeus@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Fits saturating (Michaelis-Menten type) models that link the number
    of pollinator visits to the resulting seed set in a plant population. The
    package provides tools to fit the model to empirical data, to simulate and
    fit the model when seed set saturates, to invert the model and predict the
    number of visits required to reach a given proportion of the maximum seed
    set, and to convert transect-based visit counts into the number of flowers
    visited. It is intended for ecological studies of pollination limitation
    and for power analyses that need to translate a seed set target into a
    required visitation rate.
